<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Lab Task 10</title>
    <link id="theme" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="NoStylesheet.css">
</head>
<body>
    <script src="js.js"></script>

    <div id="main-container">
        <header>
            <h1 id="one">Welcome to My Homepage</h1>
            <p id="two">Use the menu to select different Stylesheets</p>
        </header>

        <div id="semi-main">
            <div id="first-container">
                <nav>
                    <ul class="inside">
                        <li><button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet1.css')">Stylesheet 1</button></li>
                        <li><button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet2.css')">Stylesheet 2</button></li>
                        <li><button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet3.css')">Stylesheet 3</button></li>
                        <li><button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet4.css')">Stylesheet 4</button></li>
                        <li><button onclick="toggleTheme('NoStylesheet.css')">No StyleSheet</button></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

                <section>
                    <h2 id="three">Same Page Different Stylesheets</h2>
                    <p>
                        This is a demonstration of how different stylesheets can change the layout of your HTML page.
                        You can change the layout of this page by selecting different stylesheets:
                        <button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet1.css')">Stylesheet 1</button>,
                        <button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet2.css')">Stylesheet 2</button>,
                        <button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet3.css')">Stylesheet 3</button>,
                        <button onclick="toggleTheme('Stylesheet4.css')">Stylesheet 4</button>.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <article>
                    <h2 class="five">No Styles</h2>
                    <p>
                        This page uses DIV elements to group different sections of the HTML page. 
                        Click here to see how the page looks like with no stylesheet: 
                        <button onclick="toggleTheme('NoStylesheet.css')">No StyleSheet</button>.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>

            <aside>
                <h3 id="seven" class="five">Side-Bar</h3>
                <p id="six">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet...</p>
            </aside>
        </div>

        <footer>
            <p id="four">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet...</p>
        </footer>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
